CORE
integer-division.c

Passing problem to incremental SMT2 solving
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 9 negative dividend divides toward zero: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 14 negative divisor divides toward zero: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Mathematical-integer (__CPROVER_integer) division in the incremental SMT2
back-end truncates toward zero, matching div_exprt's documented semantics. The
converter builds this on top of SMT-LIB Int div (which floors) by dividing the
magnitudes and negating the quotient iff the operands have opposite signs. The
operands are symbolic (so the division reaches the solver), and the assertions
hold only under truncation -- they would fail if the floor-based SMT-LIB div
were used directly (e.g. -9 / 2 would be -5 rather than -4).
